title: The column form of a value
tags: [[Data model]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: A value's column form — its value_type and the columns that type uses — which is how the wire and a log snapshot show it.

A row's value is persisted in a ''column form'': its `value_type` and the one or two
columns that type uses (`crates/daemon/src/rows.rs`, `encode_value`/`decode_value`).
It is the form a log snapshot shows on the wire ([[Log endpoints]]). The store wrote
it too until November 2026; it now writes a compact form of its own
([[Value encoding in the store]]).

|!Column |!Holds |
|`value_type` |`nothing` · `string` · `int` · `float` · `bool` · `datetime` · `ref` · `tree_ref` · `hierarchy_ref` · `refbase` · `externalref` |
|`value_text` |`string` |
|`value_int` |`int`, `bool` (0/1), `datetime` (Unix ms) |
|`value_real` |`float` |
|`value_uuid` |`ref`/`refbase`/`externalref`: the uuid pointed at; `tree_ref`, `hierarchy_ref`: the parent (the zero uuid for a root) |
|`value_ref_repo` |`externalref`: the repository |
|`value_name` |`tree_ref`, `hierarchy_ref`: the name as displayed |
|`value_name_bytes` |`tree_ref`, `hierarchy_ref`: the name's exact bytes (its identity) |

Where the rows sit in the store: [[Store tables]].
